id: power-drain
name: Power Drain
type: standard
actionCost: 1
actionCostMax: 3
kiCost: 0
attacking: false
requiresTarget: false
special: true
usageLimit: 1/round
powerDrain: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Only as the Grappler. Up to 3 Actions, and each one takes half your Might off the
  Grappled's Life and Ki - and the Ki they actually lose comes to you.
text: >
  Power Drain Maneuver [1/Round]: Steal life force energy from an opponent.
  –Maneuver Type: Standard Maneuver
  –Action Cost: Variable
  –Minions: N/A
  –KP Cost: N/A
  –Exploitable: N/A
  –Effect: You can only use this Maneuver if you are in a Grapple Maneuver as the
  Grappler. Target the Grappled and spend up to 3 Actions. For each Action you spend,
  reduce their Life and Ki Points by 1/2 (rounded up) of your Might and regain Ki Points
  equal to the total amount of Ki Points lost by the target.

---

# --- Who may use it, and at whom ------------------------------------------------------
#
# "You can only use this Maneuver if you are in a Grapple Maneuver as the Grappler."
# Two halves and both are rules - in a Grapple at all, and the Grappler half of it - which
# is the same pair the Pin and the Launch ask, and asked the same way.
#
# "Target the Grappled" aims itself: the one you are holding is the only answer, so the
# Maneuver takes no target of its own and asking for one would be asking a question with
# one answer. The Launch does the same.
#
# --- Variable, up to three ---------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "Action Cost: Variable", and "spend up to 3 Actions" in the Effect - so the ceiling is in
# the sentence rather than in the cost line, and the floor is one. Written as a cost of 1
# with a maximum of 3, which is the shape Combat Recovery already uses; `actionCostOpen` is
# for the ones whose ceiling is only what you have left, and this one is not.
#
# --- What each Action takes ---------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "Reduce their Life and Ki Points by 1/2 (rounded up) of your Might." Rounded up, which
# almost nothing else in these rules does and this does say. Per Action, so the whole is the
# per-Action amount times the Actions - worked out as one multiplication rather than as a
# loop, because rounding once per Action is what the sentence describes and rounding once at
# the end would quietly differ on an odd Might.
#
# A Life Point reduction and a Ki Point reduction, which in these rules means straight off
# the number: past the Soak Value and the Damage Reduction, the same as a collision.
#
# --- What comes back ------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "Regain Ki Points equal to the total amount of Ki Points lost by the target." Lost, not
# taken - so a Grappled with 3 Ki Points left against a drain of 10 loses 3 and hands over
# 3. What you gain is what they actually paid, and it is capped again by your own maximum on
# the way in.
#
# The same reading Attack Absorption takes of its own "you regain Ki Points equal to", and
# for the same reason: what is regained is what there was to regain.
#
# --- How it is gained ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# A Special Maneuver, and what opens it has not been read yet.
